## 1. Scoring rubric (canonical C1-C6 × 0-10 = /60)

<!--
The 6 criteria below are the CANONICAL scoring rubric shared with
`neodoo-integrate/SKILL.md` (Phase 5). Both skills MUST use these exact
labels — do not rename or split. Scores are 0-10 per criterion; total
is 0-60.

Tier thresholds:
- T1 ≥ 50 → port immediately (story BMAD P1)
- T2 40-49 → evaluate case by case (M1, next sprint)
- T3 < 40 → do not port (reference design only)
-->

| # | Criterion | 0 | 10 |
|---|---|---|---|
| **C1** | **Compatibility** (language / framework / runtime) | Unfamiliar stack — full rewrite required | Native match (Python ↔ Odoo, TS/JS ↔ Nuxt, Go ↔ NeoGo) |
| **C2** | **Code quality** (tests, docs, idioms, readability) | Untested, undocumented, spaghetti | >80% coverage, idiomatic, well-documented |
| **C3** | **License compatibility** (SPDX, distribution model) | GPL/AGPL/proprietary → blocks proprietary SaaS distribution | MIT/Apache/BSD with attribution |
| **C4** | **Maintenance velocity** (recency, responsiveness, releases) | Stale (last commit > 18mo) or abandoned | Active (< 90d), responsive maintainers, regular releases |
| **C5** | **Dependency footprint** (new transitive deps added) | > 5 new deps or brings native C lib | ≤ 2 new deps, all already in the consumer's tree |
| **C6** | **Reversibility** (ease of unwinding the port) | Lock-in core — can't extract without surgery | Wrap/adapter pattern — trivially reversible |

**Total possible**: 60. **Thresholds**: T1 ≥ 50, T2 40-49, T3 < 40.

### 1.1 Heuristics per criterion

- **C1 (Compatibility)**: +10 if language matches one of {Python (Odoo),
  TS/JS (Nuxt), Go (NeoGo)}; +5 if minor adaptation; 0 if rewrite needed.
- **C2 (Code quality)**: anchored by coverage report and ADRs in
  `wiki/decisions.md`; +10 requires >80% coverage + ADRs + docstrings.
- **C3 (License compatibility)**: read `license-audit.md` §6 verdict
  (✅ safe = 10, ⚠️ conditional = 5, ❌ blocking = 0). LGPL dynamic
  linking OK = +5; GPL/AGPL = 0 (block).
- **C4 (Maintenance velocity)**: anchored by `git log --since="90 days
  ago"` + issue tracker activity; +10 = last commit < 30d AND open
  issues answered < 7d.
- **C5 (Dependency footprint)**: count new deps not already in the
  consumer's `package.json` / `go.mod` / `__manifest__.py`; +10 = 0–2,
  +5 = 3–5, −10 = > 5 OR adds C/Rust native lib.
- **C6 (Reversibility)**: +10 if port is a thin adapter/wrap; +5 if
  requires refactor but isolated; 0 if couples to consumer core (lock-in).

